        "original_id": "069b67c5-2a27-56e4-b8d3-b499ee03c7d2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Magazines: Vintage Life, InStyle\n- People: Rachel \"Rae\" Evans, Sarah Kate Ellis\n- Companies: Dragoon Publishing, Time Inc.\n- Places: United Kingdom, United States, Congleton, Cheshire, England\n- Topics: Fashion magazines, lifestyle magazines, vintage fashion\n\nFacts:\n- In 1994, InStyle was founded as a monthly women’s fashion magazine in the United States, and it is published by Time Inc.\n- Vintage Life is a British glossy fashion and lifestyle magazine published by Dragoon Publishing, and it focuses on the 1920s through the 1970s.\n- Sarah Kate Ellis, born on November 27, 1971, is an American media executive known for launching and turning around magazine brands including New York, InStyle, Real Simple, and Vogue.\n- Rachel \"Rae\" Evans, born on September 6, 1980, in Congleton, Cheshire, England, is the editor of Vintage Life Magazine, a British publication about vintage fashion and lifestyle from the 1920s to the 1970s.",
